==Leagues V: Raging Echoes Changes==
We're officially one week into Leagues V: Raging Echoes! While you've been blasting your way through Tasks, agonising over Relic picks and facing off against Echo bosses, our team has been working to fix those first-week bugs.

We've been keeping our [https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/leagues-v-raging-echoes---issues--fixes?oldschool=1 Issues and Fixes] blog up to date with the changes we've been able to make so far.

We've made the following coldfixes with this week's update:

* The League area emote animation now no longer hides other animations.
* There was a bug causing both the Crush Hour Combat Achievement from Phosani's Nightmare and the Temotli Triumph CA for Amoxliatl to fail.
* The Treasure Arbiter now works with the master cryptic clue featuring Juna.
* "Complete all Combat Tasks" were not registering for Vardorvis, Leviathan, Duke, Whisperer, Araxxor, and Perilous Moons despite all Combat Achievements being completed.
* We fixed a bug causing the Jewelled Crabs at CoX to switch to the wrong attack style when using Nature's Reprisal, plus roll incorrect accuracy with the melee style.
* Players with Grimoire activated can now complete the Task for redeeming an Arcane/Dex scroll, as intended.
* Fixed an issue where players couldn't get hydra or araxyte tasks.
* Equipping the Corrupted Bofa now correctly completes the regular enhanced weapon Task.

The following hotfix came earlier this week, so in case you missed it:

* Using the Total Recall orb to save a Runecrafting altar in a Region you don't have access to was causing the inability to store new memories to the orb.

We're working through bugs based on priority, so as other issues have cropped up, it's meant some of the bugs listed in the Issues & Fixes blog table are now being looked at in the following week.

